<Base title="GATE 2027 eligibility" description="Who can apply for GATE 2027: how to check eligibility in the official brochure and what categories of students should verify." canonicalPath="/gate-2027/eligibility/">
  <section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Editorial summary · brochure is authoritative</p>
    <h1>GATE 2027 eligibility</h1>
    <p class="lead">Do not rely on coaching blogs for eligibility. Check the current official information brochure — it is the only authoritative source for degree qualifications, year-of-study rules and category requirements.</p>
    <div class="btn-row"><a class="btn primary" href="https://gate2027.iitm.ac.in/" rel="noopener">Open official site</a><a class="btn ghost" href="/gate-2027/application/">Application guide</a></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap grid cols-2">
    <div class="card"><h3>How to verify (5 minutes)</h3><ol><li>Open the official brochure PDF from the GATE 2027 site.</li><li>Find the eligibility section; match your degree + year.</li><li>Check ID, photo, signature and certificate requirements.</li><li>If unsure, use the official helpdesk — not social media.</li></ol></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Common cases to double-check</h3><ul><li>Final-year students vs completed degrees</li><li>Backlogs / pending results</li><li>Distance / AMIE-type qualifications</li><li>International / NRI applicants</li><li>Name / DOB mismatches across IDs</li></ul></div>
  </div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="source-box">Source: <a href="https://gate2027.iitm.ac.in/" rel="noopener">gate2027.iitm.ac.in</a> · Last verified 2026-09-11. <a href="/report-error/">Report an error</a>.</div></div></section>
</Base>
